<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 13 July, from 982 to 1923.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">982</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kalbid army defeats Emperor Otto II at Stilo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The forces of the Kalbid emir of Sicily routed Otto II's army near Stilo in Calabria, though the emir himself was killed. Otto barely escaped by swimming to a ship, and his plans to conquer southern Italy collapsed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1174</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William the Lion of Scotland is captured at Alnwick</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English knights surprised King William I of Scotland in fog outside Alnwick and took him prisoner. To win his release he accepted the Treaty of Falaise, submitting Scotland to Henry II's overlordship.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1787</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress passes the Northwest Ordinance</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Confederation Congress set out how lands north-west of the Ohio River would be governed and admitted as new states. It also banned slavery there, shaping the pattern of American westward expansion.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1837</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria moves into Buckingham Palace</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three weeks after her accession, 18-year-old Victoria became the first monarch to live at Buckingham Palace. It has been the sovereign's principal London residence ever since.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1878</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Berlin redraws the map of the Balkans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress of Berlin recognised the independence of Serbia, Montenegro and Romania and cut back the large Bulgaria created by Russia. Its compromises left grievances that fed later Balkan wars.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1923</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Hollywoodland sign is dedicated in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A giant sign reading 'Hollywoodland' was unveiled in the hills above Los Angeles to advertise a housing development. Shortened to 'Hollywood' in 1949, it became a global symbol of the film industry.</p></li></ol>
